        "created_at": "2022-07-31T18:05:10.126Z",
        "cooked": "<p><em>The other day, I was rummaging around in my attic, and I found my old collection of Sentinel Comics Trading Cards from the ‘90s! So I thought I’d post them here for all of you.</em></p>\n<p>Okay, so that didn’t actually happen. Sentinel Comics never made trading cards in the ‘90s. However, a <a href=\"https://www.marvel.com/\">lesser-know comics company</a> did actually make a series of trading cards. And on the backs of those cards were Power Ratings: numerical rankings of characters’ powers, skills, and abilities.</p>\n<p>So, I thought that it would be fun to make Power Ratings for the Sentinel Comics characters.</p>\n<p>Here’s how the system works. There are six attributes: <strong>Fighting Ability</strong>, <strong>Intelligence</strong>, <strong>Strength</strong>, <strong>Speed</strong>, <strong>Durability</strong>, and <strong>Energy Projection</strong>. Every character’s attributes are ranked on a scale from 1 (below average) to 7 (godlike). In most cases, 2 is the human average. More details are available here: <a href=\"https://marvel.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Grid\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Power Grid | Marvel Database | Fandom</a></p>\n<p>And here are my ratings for all of the Sentinel Comics heroes: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1iZ073schHrVxeoM3JEjjuQQe_mauKUt6ErpZfHA5ZqM/edit\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Sentinel Comics Trading Cards - Google Sheets</a></p>\n<p>I may get around to the villains in the future; time will tell.</p>\n<p>Of course, we all know that trying to quantify and rank the superpowers of comic characters is a fool’s errand. The powers and abilities of such characters fluctuate wildly from issue to issue. Nonetheless, I did this just for fun, so here I am.</p>\n<p>Well, what do you think? Did I get the rankings right? Am I way off? Should Character X actually be stronger than Character Y? I’d love to hear your thoughts.</p>\n<p>Let the discussions and debates begin!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
